10220.sol:
Let the equation of tangent to the parabola $y^2=x$, having slope $m$ is, y=m x+$\frac{1}{4 m}$ For common tangent to the circle x²+y²-6 y+4=0 $\therefore$ Radius $\sqrt{9-4}=\frac{\left|3-\frac{1}{4 m}\right|}{\sqrt{1+m^2}} $\begin{array}{rlrl}
\Rightarrow& 5 $\left(1+m²\right)$ & =9+$\frac{1}{16 m^2}-\frac{3}{2 m}$\\
\Rightarrow & & m & =$\frac{1}{2}$
\end{array}$ So, equation of common tangent is $\begin{aligned} y & =$\frac{1}{2}$ x+$\frac{1}{2}$\\
\Rightarrow \quad x-2 y+1 & =0 .
\end{aligned}

